      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Authenticity here comes from rooting the enterprise within existing community needs or power vacuums. Instead of framing it as purely self-serving greed, explore how the narcotics trade might intersect with local economic exclusion, offering a perceived form of localized power or success where traditional avenues are blocked. The dynamics should reflect complex hierarchies within the community, perhaps involving codes of loyalty, familial obligations, or leveraging established informal economic networks. This approach positions the character as a product of their environment's limitations, not just a cartoon criminal.",
